# Vue / JS / UI

## Components

- Composition API with `<script setup>` at the top
- PascalCase components, camelCase events
- PropTypes for props; ESLint (Airbnb + Vue 3 recommended)
- No bare strings in templates — use i18n (`useI18n`); locale paths in `chatwoot-core.mdc`
- Business logic in composables or store actions — thin components for presentation

## Async permission / membership context

Gates that depend on store memberships (inboxes, teams, etc.):

- `loading` ≠ `loaded empty` — do not treat an empty list as “no access” while fetch is in flight
- While `isFetching` (or equivalent) is true, do not fail-closed on empty memberships — trust backend-scoped data or show loading
- Fail-closed only after fetch completed with no memberships

## Styling — Tailwind only

- No custom CSS, scoped CSS, or inline styles
- Use Tailwind utilities; colors from `tailwind.config.js`

```vue
<!-- ❌ --><div style="color: red" class="my-custom-class">
<!-- ✅ --><div class="text-red-500 bg-n-background p-4 rounded-lg">
```

## Example

```vue
<script setup>
import { computed } from 'vue';
import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n';

const { t } = useI18n();
const label = computed(() => t('CONVERSATION.HEADER'));
</script>

<template>
  <span>{{ label }}</span>
</template>
```
